CM Dipole in free space
CM
CM ! Written by EZNEC/Pro+ v. 7.0 in NEC-2 format.
CM
CM ! Wire #2 for I srcs, shorted/open TL, and/or parallel loads.
CM ! NT #1 is EZNEC current source
CM
CM 	Dipole1
CM 
CM This is a plain dipole in free space, about the simplest antenna you're
CM likely to model. The frequency is 299.7+ MHz (selected by entering '0'
CM for the frequency), at which a wavelength is one meter. The antenna
CM dimensions, in meters, are therefore also the dimensions in wavelengths.
CM Note that this antenna, exactly a half wavelength long, is greater than
CM a resonant length, as indicated by the positive feedpoint reactance
CM (seen by clicking the Control Center Src Dat [Source Data] action
CM button. A resonant "half-wave" antenna is somewhat shorter than 0.5
CM wavelength, the amount depending on its diameter.
CE
GW 1,11,0.,-.25,0.,0.,.25,0.,.0005
GW 2,3,99.99998,99.99998,99.99998,100.003,100.003,100.003,1.0000E-4
GE 0
FR 0,1,0,0,299.7925
GN -1
EX 0,2,2,0,0.,1.414214
NT 2,2,1,6,0.,0.,0.,1.,0.,0.
RP 0,1,361,1000,90.,0.,0.,1.,0.
EN
